{"timestamp":"2026-05-30T02:51:25.756Z","level":"info","source":"model","message":"response","data":{"model":"qwen36-35b","text":"\n\nI've loaded the **VoidRift Blueprint** (`blueprint.md`). Here's a summary of what this document defines:\n\n## VoidRift: Decoupled Subsystem Architecture\n\n### What It Is\nVoidRift is a **highly decoupled, model-agnostic monorepo AI engineering harness** designed as a local developer tool. It combines a multi-agent orchestrator with a terminal-based UI (TUI) built in React and Ink.\n\n### Key Philosophy\n- **Local-First & Model Agnostic** — Runs local open-weight models (Ollama, vLLM, Llama.cpp) and cloud models (DeepSeek, Gemini, Anthropic, OpenAI) alike\n- **Rate-Limit & Cost Freedom** — Zero rate-limit anxiety for local execution; prefix caching minimizes cloud costs\n- **Sovereign Developer** — Secure, predictable, no cloud lock-in\n\n### Five Architectural Pillars\n1. **Pure Composition Root & Event Bus** — Parallel systems communicate via async events, not direct calls\n2. **Three-Partition Context** — Segregates context into Governance (static), Workspace (semi-dynamic), and Work (volatile","toolCalls":[],"usage":{"promptTokens":4730,"completionTokens":645,"totalTokens":5375}}}
